{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790024817,"nonce":"T5LOGFX/kSLGtK1pAkC1+O8bQd4=","message":"From the config entity design (doc/design/config-entity.md, 3556569): when the sync changes the schema (Jira added a status, renamed a priority) it goes through the same reconcile(desired, current) as schema import, executed inside cache.ConfigCache.Update so the diff is against the re-read entity, one commit per sync pass, and only when something differs (E6, E10). Canonical JSON (sorted keys, normalised numbers) is the comparison, which is the 'normalise before comparing' rule from 7c90fbd. Open for this task: where the Jira field-id \u003c-\u003e schema-key mapping itself lives — git config like today's bridge configs, or a section of the config entity so it syncs with the tracker. The entity has room (a section needs an owner and a validator, E6); decide here.","files":null}]}